            <ArticleTitle>Foot claudication with plantar flexion as a result of dorsalis pedis artery impingement in an Irish dancer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>212-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jvs.2012.11.037</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0741-5214(12)02407-X</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dorsalis pedis artery impingement is an extremely rare cause of foot claudication, with a single case reported in the literature. In this report, we describe the case of a 17-year-old female Irish dancer who presented with intermittent bilateral foot pain and discoloration during active plantar flexion.</AbstractText>
